{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_adr_006_mysql_generated_columns", "label": "ADR-006: MySQL Generated Columns for Derived Financial Values", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/006-mysql-generated-columns.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Computing derived financial fields (berat_ton, berat_rata_janjang, total_pendapatan, hasil_bersih, pendapatan_bersih) in the application layer or as manually-updated columns risks divergence from source columns across multiple write paths. Chose MySQL `GENERATED ALWAYS AS (...) STORED` columns so the DB engine guarantees consistency by construction, can be indexed, and appears in SELECT *, with zero application logic. Trade-off: changing a formula requires a migration; STORED columns use disk space like regular columns; developers unfamiliar with generated columns may try to INSERT/UPDATE them and hit a confusing MySQL error (documented in handler comments); division-by-zero (jumlah_janjang=0) correctly resolves to NULL."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_adr_006_mysql_generated_columns", "target": "docs_architecture_system_architecture", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/006-mysql-generated-columns.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_006_mysql_generated_columns", "target": "docs_database_schema_explained_t_sawit_hub_panen", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/006-mysql-generated-columns.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_006_mysql_generated_columns", "target": "docs_database_schema_explained_t_sawit_hub_pendapatan", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/006-mysql-generated-columns.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_006_mysql_generated_columns", "